### Problem

An **unread first completion** can be suppressed from the parent model solely because another parent tool call lasts long enough. The task and report remain retrievable, but the completion becomes a TUI-only custom entry, without a model-facing message or wake request. The parent can then say it is still awaiting verification and become idle until a human intervenes.

This is a narrowly scoped follow-up to #867 / #913, not a request to restore stale replay. #867 concerned already-consumed results. PR #913 explicitly acknowledges the long-turn tradeoff; this report supplies an unread-result occurrence and deterministic component evidence for that branch.

**Observed retained evidence, task identities omitted (UTC, 2026-09-16):**

| Time | Observation |
|---|---|
| 03:12:35.013 | Parent receives background verifier launch confirmation. |
| 03:13:29.999 | Parent starts synchronous `subagent_continue` for a different task. |
| 03:13:41.314 | Verifier session records final assistant message, `stopReason: stop`. |
| 03:13:41.430 | Retained verifier metadata records `completed`, 13 turns, 20 tool calls, no error. |
| 03:15:22.954 | Parent's synchronous tool returns after approximately 113 seconds. |
| 03:15:22.955 | Parent appends `custom` / `gentle-agents.stale-result`, `ageSeconds: 102`. |
| 03:17:48.706 | Parent says independent verification is pending, without checking status. |
| 03:22:04.927 | Human asks why work stopped. |
| 03:22:13–18 | Parent queries status and retrieves the completed report. |

Across the inspected transcript, this task has one stale entry and zero `gentle-agents.result` messages. A successful control task in the same session completed at 03:11:21.461 and received its normal completion message at 03:11:21.466, followed by parent activity. No compaction or branch-summary entry appears in the incident interval.

**Source trace:** `agent_end` retains the report; `agent_settled` allows terminal handling; the runner confirms process exit, updates task state and calls `onFinish`. The extension requests persistence and enqueues completion. A busy parent flushes at a turn/run boundary. `takeDeliverable()` classifies still-unconsumed completions aged >=90 seconds as stale and marks them delivered. `deliverStale()` uses `appendEntry`, not `sendMessage`. Pi documents custom entries as excluded from LLM context.

Source references at the examined revision:
- [Threshold and consume/deliver bookkeeping](https://github.com/Gentleman-Programming/gentle-shell/blob/657e532997e13ac196a0ad1e01329fc1163ffd69/lib/agents-completion-delivery.ts#L13-L63)
- [Delivery and lifecycle flush wiring](https://github.com/Gentleman-Programming/gentle-shell/blob/657e532997e13ac196a0ad1e01329fc1163ffd69/extensions/gentle-agents.ts#L803-L863)
- [Persistence request and completion enqueue](https://github.com/Gentleman-Programming/gentle-shell/blob/657e532997e13ac196a0ad1e01329fc1163ffd69/extensions/gentle-agents.ts#L898-L923)

**Limits:** raw historical RPC event timestamps and the exact revision loaded into the historical processes were not captured. The timeline observes persisted messages/task state; lifecycle internals are a source trace. The parent also omitted a final status check, but there is no evidence it received and ignored this completion message. This report does not establish a Herdr, provider, or Pi scheduler defect. #1001/#1034 concern startup/watchdog failures, #1028 print-mode exit, and #626 aggregate Herdr status; those are distinct.

The queue file is byte-identical in published `v2.7.0` and inspected remote `main` `002c98101972aefe437fad1669a80a43bb930791` (Git blob `90a8f4d997e458c563a83c450bc2384cdc42788a`). That main revision also retains the stale `appendEntry` branch. No published fix for this unread-first-delivery case was identified.

